1
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:13,340
Try letting peace go, light and free.

2
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:26,880
Aiming for that day
drifting on the Nakagawa,

3
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:33,980
kick a pebble and even your shoes fly off.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,300
So, to the head carpenter
who'd been saving up,

5
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed that you're still just a kid.

6
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if I leave some energy somewhere,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,620
in Katsushika, a sigh,
a yawn, nothing changes.

8
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:02,500
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

9
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,480
From the pointed hat's water bottle,

10
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:16,800
the setting sun falls toward the vast sky.

11
00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:25,240
Tomorrow too, it'll end just like this

12
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:30,400
Shibamata again, even happiness gets lost.

13
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:34,020
Because I'm a fool who got carried away.

14
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:41,360
Transform! The Chief's new car!

15
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:00,500
Hey, don't you want to see the set?

16
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:01,980
Excuse me.

17
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:06,300
Mister, watch it!

18
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:08,340
S-sorry.

19
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:11,720
Eek!

20
00:02:13,380 --> 00:02:15,220
Don't touch my butt!

21
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:19,720
It wasn't me!
How could I touch you in this position!

22
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:22,800
Now that you mention it, you're right.

23
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:30,380
I-I'm getting off at my stop...

24
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:46,380
Why is this commuter train so crowded?

25
00:02:51,340 --> 00:02:52,220
Nakagawa

26
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:58,560
I want to commute by car too.

27
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:04,000
The Chief is buying a car?

28
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:08,160
I've truly had enough of
commuting by train today.

29
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,840
Packed trains every morning for over two hours,
no less.

30
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:14,000
Not much of a role, is it?

31
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:17,440
Since Reiko is on paid leave,
I'm the stand-in.

32
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:18,520
Thanks.

33
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:22,680
That's why I told you not to
build a house in such a backwater.

34
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:25,580
It's too late to say that now.

35
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:29,860
Speaking of which, Chief,
I have a car I've only driven a few times.

36
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:35,940
I'll give it to you. Really?
Wow, Kei-chan, you're generous!

37
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:45,980
Well, I accidentally bought two cars of the same color.
So what kind of car is it? A yellow Porsche. A yellow Porsche.

38
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:54,840
A Porsche would cost over 10 million yen. I can't
accept such an expensive car worth 10 million.

39
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:58,180
Why not?
If it were me, I'd gladly accept it.

40
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:02,300
Idiot! With the morals of public
servants under scrutiny right now,

41
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:07,620
even if it's from a subordinate,
I can't accept such a luxury car, can I?

42
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:09,420
What a waste.

43
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:12,600
So how much are you
planning to spend on one?

44
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:15,340
Well, around 500,000 yen, I suppose.

45
00:04:15,340 --> 00:04:18,860
Then you can't even afford a new kei car.

46
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:20,320
A used car is fine.

47
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:25,100
Even though my subordinates Nakagawa and Reiko
are driving around in Ferraris and Porsches.

48
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:27,020
The Chief buying a used car

49
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:31,020
Don't tell me that,
you who ride around on a bicycle.

50
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:36,120
Anyway, it has nothing to do with me.

51
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:40,520
Wait, is this a chance to make some money?

52
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:45,080
You got me there.

53
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:46,960
Understood, Chief.

54
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:49,660
Let me help you pick out a used car.

55
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,440
No way!

56
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:55,140
If I take you along, even a deal
that's already settled will fall apart.

57
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:56,120
No.

58
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,480
But, Chief,

59
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:01,380
no one has a better talent
for haggling than Ryo-sama.

60
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:03,220
Still,

61
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:05,460
when Terai picked out his house,

62
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:07,600
and when the station
went on its overseas trip,

63
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:10,280
he really drove the prices down, didn't he?

64
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:12,800
That's true.

65
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:16,500
You'll haggle properly, won't you, Ryo-chan?

66
00:05:17,220 --> 00:05:18,540
Leave it to me.

67
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:28,020
Alright, time to open the new company!

68
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:29,740
We'll sell, sell, and sell some more!

69
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:42,220
Phew, looks like today's going to be fine.

70
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:47,580
Hey there.

71
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:48,680
Hehehe!

72
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:50,780
Aren't you that tourist from before?

73
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:54,040
So now you've started a
bogus used car business?

74
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:57,840
P-please don't say such unpopular things!

75
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:01,220
We're an honest shop that
prides itself on sincerity.

76
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:02,960
I can't trust you, though.

77
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:05,040
Well, I suppose I'll look at the cars.

78
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:06,500
What a shame.

79
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,600
We're closed today.

80
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:09,940
Don't lie!

81
00:06:09,940 --> 00:06:12,360
Your opening day can't
possibly be a day off!

82
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:14,380
That's, well, the thing is...

83
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:19,060
We're trying to be your very first customer,
you know.

84
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:20,960
Hurry up and show us around.

85
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,560
If your budget is 500,000 yen,

86
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:26,980
how about this car?

87
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:28,160
How about it?

88
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:29,460
It's spotless!

89
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:32,560
It really is beautiful.

90
00:06:32,560 --> 00:06:33,940
It looks brand new.

91
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:36,400
They repainted the whole thing
to hide the junk underneath,

92
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,720
so let's go with it!

93
00:06:39,380 --> 00:06:47,000
How about this one? It's only been driven 6,000 km.
Ryotsu, right? It's still practically new!

94
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:57,720
A '93 model, five years old, with only 6,000 km?
That's suspicious. *Gulp* I have no idea what you're talking about.

95
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:03,180
Chief, I want to check the engine,
so please open the hood switch.

96
00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:06,660
What is this engine?

97
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:09,560
I can't believe it's
only been driven 6,000 km.

98
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:13,400
The odometer must have
gone around twice, right?

99
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:16,700
Not at all, it's only gone around once.

100
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,280
Oh no, I've been caught.

101
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:22,560
So that means it's been driven 106,000 km?

102
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:26,360
This guy is a total fraud.

103
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:28,520
Good people of the neighborhood,

104
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:31,260
this used car center is

105
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,280
I'm a pro too.

106
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:38,180
In that case,
I'll show you our super bargain.

107
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:39,780
Super bargain?

108
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:43,580
It's a two-year-old model,
fully equipped, and this is the price.

109
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:47,240
You won't find a deal like
this anywhere in Japan.

110
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:48,660
And the engine, too.

111
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:53,320
The engine does seem to be in good shape,
I suppose.

112
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:57,180
Not bad, but 698,000 yen

113
00:07:57,960 --> 00:07:58,760
Understood.

114
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:06,680
Since you're our first customer of the day,
we'll give you a huge discount.

115
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:09,800
Is that true or not, Ryotsu?

116
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:18,160
The bumper's been replaced with a new one,
but the license plate is dented.

117
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:19,760
This car's been in an accident, hasn't it.

118
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:23,220
Gulp... I'm not joking, you know.

119
00:08:23,220 --> 00:08:26,480
If you bought this new,
it'd cost over 2 million yen.

120
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:31,400
This might be a car that's hit
several people in an accident.

121
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:33,520
Nothing like that, never.

122
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,420
What are you doing?

123
00:08:40,420 --> 00:08:43,040
I'm summoning the spirit
that's attached to this car.

124
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,400
Three of them, too.

125
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:47,900
The chassis was just
bent out of shape as well.

126
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:49,600
It's an accident car after all, isn't it!

127
00:08:50,060 --> 00:08:51,080
It rolled over.

128
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:54,560
Pulling your crooked tricks again,
you bastard!

129
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:58,680
Please, cut me some slack, you!

130
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:03,120
Isn't that a Volkswagen Beetle?

131
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:04,620
Brings back memories.

132
00:09:05,300 --> 00:09:07,520
There's no price on it.
How much is this one?

133
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:11,040
That one's my own car. It's not for sale.

134
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:13,840
Oh, is that so?

135
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:18,140
Well, when I was young,
I always dreamed of driving one of these.

136
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:20,320
You have a fine car.

137
00:09:20,780 --> 00:09:21,660
Th-thanks.

138
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:26,340
The Chief likes it so much,
just sell it to him!

139
00:09:26,340 --> 00:09:29,460
I already told you, that one's not for sale!

140
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:37,140
Ladies and gentlemen, every car at this
used car center is an accident car...

141
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:38,880
Please stop.

142
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:41,000
So you'll sell it to us?

143
00:09:41,620 --> 00:09:42,880
Fine, I understand.

144
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:47,280
But that car has cost over 500,000 yen just to fix up for the restaurant,
you know.

145
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:49,340
Unless it's around a million.

146
00:09:49,340 --> 00:09:51,160
Ladies and gentlemen,

147
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:54,680
Fine, I'll sell it to you for 500,000 yen.

148
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:56,100
I see.

149
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:58,960
Ryotsu,
what have you been doing this whole time?

150
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:02,840
Chief, good news!
They're willing to sell it to us.

151
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:08,000
Really? But didn't you say
earlier it was your own car?

152
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:15,540
We don't have cars to spare, you know! I'm negotiating the price right now,
so please wait a little longer.

153
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:18,560
Is that so? That's very kind of you.

154
00:10:20,420 --> 00:10:22,834
I taught that customer a lesson. Naturally,

155
00:10:22,884 --> 00:10:25,020
the medical expenses will be covered, right?

156
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,320
N-no joke!

157
00:10:27,370 --> 00:10:30,340
I've already lost 500,000 yen, you know!

158
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:31,780
You must be joking!

159
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:33,420
Whoa! Alright, alright!

160
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:39,297
Well then. Well,

161
00:10:39,347 --> 00:10:41,920
don't lose heart, and keep your chin up.

162
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:44,040
Gulp... th-thank you very much!

163
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:51,340
Damn it!

164
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:53,660
He took a 10% cut and lined his own pockets,
the bastard!

165
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:55,900
Somebody bring me salt!

166
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:02,460
The engine seems to be in pretty good shape,
doesn't it?

167
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:05,440
But it's not a fire truck, you know.

168
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:07,180
The bright red colour is a bit much, though.

169
00:11:07,180 --> 00:11:10,060
I haggled it down from a million to five hundred thousand for you,
after all!

170
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:11,920
Don't complain, please.

171
00:11:15,380 --> 00:11:17,680
Isn't that Chief over there?

172
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:18,840
Really.

173
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:20,340
Chief

174
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:24,160
What happened? Is this bright red car yours?

175
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:27,100
Yes, I just bought it.

176
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:31,700
Wow, the shape is unique too, and the
bright red makes it look kind of stylish.

177
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:33,540
You think so?

178
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:36,940
That's exactly why I bought it.

179
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:40,340
Why don't you two come for
a drive with me sometime?

180
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:41,700
Really?

181
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,200
We're looking forward to it.

182
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:44,940
Well then,

183
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:46,320
Yes, take care.

184
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:53,540
Well, the red one looks pretty good too,
doesn't it?

185
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:56,360
Chief, what kind of
personality do you have, anyway?

186
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:57,440
No, no.

187
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:03,240
A VW Beetle? That's a pretty classic choice.

188
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:09,660
Right? The engine runs well too, so they
say I can drive it for another ten years.

189
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:13,000
You take good care of your things,
Chief, so you'll be fine.

190
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:16,800
Chief, you have a call
from the Station Chief.

191
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:18,680
I'm coming right away.

192
00:12:19,340 --> 00:12:22,720
Next time, let's take Nakagawa's
car and go for a drive around Nikko.

193
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:23,540
Sounds great.

194
00:12:23,980 --> 00:12:25,800
Though we might get a little
too carried away with excitement.

195
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:28,300
Hey! What do you think you're doing?!

196
00:12:29,740 --> 00:12:31,540
Ryo-san! Grab the ball!

197
00:12:31,840 --> 00:12:34,380
Alright! Leave it to me!

198
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:35,900
Senpai!

199
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:37,640
Ryo-chan's deadly hand!

200
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:40,900
Thanks, Ryo-san!

201
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:45,200
Impressive, senpai! Your years
of cycling experience really show!

202
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:47,460
Are you okay?

203
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:51,280
S-senpai, are you all right?

204
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:53,020
Th-the, th-the, tr-tree, tr-tree...

205
00:12:53,660 --> 00:12:54,080
What?

206
00:12:55,780 --> 00:12:56,360
Run!

207
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:59,260
S-senpai, this is bad.

208
00:12:59,260 --> 00:13:01,800
I see. Actually...

209
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:04,841
If the Chief sees this,

210
00:13:04,891 --> 00:13:07,220
he'll turn into Daimajin!

211
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:10,400
What do we do?!

212
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:26,480
Regarding that matter,
at the squad leaders' meeting the other day,

213
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:29,360
What are you doing?

214
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:32,040
What's wrong?

215
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:34,300
Things have gotten a bit dicey.

216
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,160
If that's the case,

217
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,060
Yes, understood.

218
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:42,820
Right, this should be good enough.

219
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:45,440
Now for the textured plastic paint,

220
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:49,000
There, that should be fine, right?

221
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:52,200
It's not fine at all.

222
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:54,080
Take a good look.

223
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,280
It stands out even more.

224
00:13:58,820 --> 00:14:02,180
In that case, should we just
paint over the door with this?

225
00:14:04,940 --> 00:14:06,560
Damn, we ran out.

226
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:10,200
If so, let's paint over it with this.

227
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:12,880
This one too?

228
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:16,500
Well then, how about this?

229
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:20,680
I'm not giving up again!

230
00:14:24,980 --> 00:14:26,040
How about this?

231
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:28,460
It's not even recognizable anymore.

232
00:14:28,460 --> 00:14:29,600
This is the worst.

233
00:14:32,860 --> 00:14:33,700
You.

234
00:14:33,700 --> 00:14:36,900
What do we do?

235
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:39,540
I know a repair shop nearby,

236
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:42,400
so we should have them repaint it.

237
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:44,740
We finally made 50,000 yen, you know!

238
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:45,700
50,000 yen?

239
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:47,880
Nothing, never mind.

240
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:49,380
Alright, let's go there.

241
00:14:49,380 --> 00:14:51,340
I'll go borrow the keys from the Chief.

242
00:14:53,620 --> 00:14:55,880
Chief, I have a quick favor to ask.

243
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:56,340
What is it?

244
00:14:56,340 --> 00:14:59,000
I'd really love to take
a ride in that classic car.

245
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,920
Nakagawa will do the driving.

246
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:03,700
Can we go for a three-hour drive?

247
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:06,040
You're hopeless.

248
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:09,080
Well, if Nakagawa's driving,
it should be fine.

249
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:11,000
Just don't crash it.

250
00:15:13,100 --> 00:15:16,120
Of course, rest assured.

251
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:21,160
We'll get it fixed in the three
hours before Nakagawa gets back.

252
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,580
Then let's hurry.

253
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:34,740
Senpai,

254
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:39,440
I heard the chief went
out to eat and isn't here...

255
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:41,260
We can't just let him not be here!

256
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:42,880
Go find him, no matter what!

257
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:44,340
Understood.

258
00:15:44,340 --> 00:15:47,000
Then, senpai, please wait in the car.

259
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:48,700
Honestly...

260
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:51,320
Because the chief lost his mind
and bought a private car like this.

261
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:52,560
That's why we're in this mess.

262
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:54,320
Ah ah...

263
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:56,240
Guess I'll sleep until the chief gets back.

264
00:15:56,680 --> 00:15:57,040
Yeah.

265
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:13,760
Which one is Mr. Yamada's car that
the president told us to crush?

266
00:16:14,260 --> 00:16:17,900
Isn't it this one?
It's dirty and the model's old too.

267
00:16:18,640 --> 00:16:19,680
Right, let's move it.

268
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:21,760
Okay, okay, back it up.

269
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:25,760
Stop.

270
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:34,800
It doesn't look like an accident car.

271
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:37,800
Never mind the paint, the rest is solid.

272
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:38,900
It's bad luck, though.

273
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:41,120
Didn't the owner get shot?

274
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:43,760
Chief, this way.

275
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:44,280
Yes.

276
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:47,520
Senpai?

277
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:50,600
Mr. Yamada's car is still here.

278
00:16:51,440 --> 00:16:52,660
I wonder where they went?

279
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:54,180
The car's gone too?

280
00:17:02,740 --> 00:17:04,400
What was that jolt?

281
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,080
Stop rocking like an idiot!

282
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:09,240
It's an earthquake!

283
00:17:12,420 --> 00:17:13,860
Hey, look, stop!

284
00:17:13,860 --> 00:17:14,960
There's someone inside!

285
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:15,740
Stop!

286
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:17,940
That's a total mess!

287
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:19,720
Stop for a second!

288
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:20,800
Boss!

289
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:23,120
There's a person inside the van!

290
00:17:26,260 --> 00:17:27,140
Senpai!

291
00:17:27,140 --> 00:17:29,180
Get me out of here already!

292
00:17:29,180 --> 00:17:30,680
Thank goodness.

293
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:31,940
They're still alive.

294
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:34,680
Please burn through the
car body and rescue them.

295
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:37,420
I-I can't believe it.

296
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:43,180
Ow

297
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,800
I woke up and suddenly got crushed!

298
00:17:45,800 --> 00:17:47,480
What on earth is going on?

299
00:17:48,260 --> 00:17:49,700
Good thing you're safe.

300
00:17:50,220 --> 00:17:52,240
How did you survive in that space?

301
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:54,840
He's like the second Tenkō Hikida.

302
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:56,440
Huh?

303
00:17:56,700 --> 00:18:00,300
Whoa! The Chief's Beetle
has turned into a pill bug!

304
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:33,360
How about it?
Doesn't it look just like the original?

305
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:35,720
The sizes are completely different.

306
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:38,860
Shut up! We only have two hours left!

307
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:40,680
Never mind the small details.

308
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:44,120
But boss, this engine's dead.

309
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:47,320
Then we'll just have to
put in a different one.

310
00:18:47,320 --> 00:18:49,700
Then put in the engine from that Porsche.

311
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:51,520
That's totally unreasonable.

312
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:55,340
Putting a Porsche's 300-horsepower engine in a Subaru?
That's crazy.

313
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:59,200
Shut up! With 300 horsepower,
the Chief will be thrilled too.

314
00:18:59,940 --> 00:19:02,440
And don't forget the
Volkswagen emblem, either.

315
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:04,100
Understood.

316
00:19:05,420 --> 00:19:06,980
I wonder if this will really be okay.

317
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:17,500
Leaving early like this must be tough.

318
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,300
But I think they'll find out right away.

319
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:22,020
We'll cross that bridge when we come to it.

320
00:19:22,020 --> 00:19:22,720
Let's go.

321
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:23,300
Ryotsu!

322
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:27,100
So, how was the ride?

323
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:30,700
The ride was top-notch!

324
00:19:30,700 --> 00:19:35,580
It felt so good, I thought I was
going straight to the afterlife.

325
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:37,520
Is that so, is that so.

326
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:41,120
It seems a little smaller somehow.

327
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:43,860
What are you talking about, Chief?

328
00:19:43,860 --> 00:19:46,820
The Beetle has always been this size,
hasn't it?

329
00:19:47,880 --> 00:19:50,400
It's because you're
looking at it from far away.

330
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:52,500
Take a closer look.

331
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:54,820
It looks bigger, doesn't it?

332
00:19:54,820 --> 00:19:57,800
It's just an optical
illusion from perspective.

333
00:19:58,300 --> 00:20:00,300
I see. I was mistaken.

334
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:03,600
The mirror's shape is different.

335
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:06,300
Come on, it's the same. Look.

336
00:20:06,820 --> 00:20:10,240
Even the emblem is exactly the same Volkswagen one,
isn't it?

337
00:20:10,780 --> 00:20:12,140
True, that's right.

338
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:16,260
Wasn't the door supposed to open like this?

339
00:20:16,740 --> 00:20:19,320
Chief, you're always joking.

340
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:21,940
Everyone knows the Beetle's
doors open from the front.

341
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:23,260
I see.

342
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:25,785
Nakagawa,

343
00:20:25,835 --> 00:20:29,720
we can't keep goofing off forever.

344
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:31,820
Let's go on patrol or something.

345
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:32,880
Y-yes, sir.

346
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:34,560
Wait!

347
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:38,360
Ryotsu, the steering wheel's
switched to the right side!

348
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:42,020
N-no good, Senpai. We can't hide it anymore.

349
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:46,520
Come on, Chief,
it's been right-hand drive from the start.

350
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:49,360
My car, what happened to...

351
00:20:49,360 --> 00:20:52,180
No, I mean, this...
this is the Chief's car...

352
00:20:52,180 --> 00:20:53,740
No! That's not my car!

353
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:58,700
Look! See, it has a Porsche engine in it!

354
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:04,460
That's amazing!
Now the Chief's a drag racer too! So cool!

355
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:08,260
What happened to my car?

356
00:21:08,460 --> 00:21:12,120
Well, once you're driving this,
the gyarus won't leave you alone!

357
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:15,000
I'm asking what happened to my car!

358
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:17,683
Your car but,

359
00:21:17,733 --> 00:21:21,000
It's better not to look,
for your own health...

360
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:24,160
Just bring it here already!

361
00:21:24,820 --> 00:21:26,320
Okay, okay, okay!

362
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:28,040
Stop!

363
00:21:29,020 --> 00:21:31,140
Well then, we'll be going now.

364
00:21:39,220 --> 00:21:41,960
So this is my car?

365
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:45,700
It's changed shape a little...

366
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:48,120
But you can still see traces of it.

367
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:49,940
That's the left door over there,

368
00:21:49,940 --> 00:21:51,860
and the black part is the engine.

369
00:21:51,860 --> 00:21:54,080
Senpai, stop it!

370
00:21:54,820 --> 00:21:57,940
Making it into a stone for hunting, or other uses,
there are all sorts of ways to use it...

371
00:21:59,100 --> 00:22:01,760
You bastard!

372
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:03,380
Nakagawa, we're in trouble!

373
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:04,080
Run!

374
00:22:08,780 --> 00:22:09,840
I won't let you get away!

375
00:22:14,300 --> 00:22:15,920
Hey! What is this car?!

376
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:18,460
It's doing a wheelie the whole time!

377
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:23,000
It's lifting off the ground because the
high-horsepower engine doesn't match the body!

378
00:22:28,280 --> 00:22:30,700
No good! Senpai! The steering won't respond!

379
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:32,820
We can only go straight like this!

380
00:22:33,040 --> 00:22:33,280
What?

381
00:22:35,940 --> 00:22:40,080
Aw, crap! They've caught up!
Chief! That's speeding, you know!

382
00:22:40,380 --> 00:22:42,860
Shut up! You're the ones getting arrested!

383
00:22:44,580 --> 00:22:46,240
Stop! Stop, damn it!

384
00:22:47,300 --> 00:22:49,000
They're saying that, so let's stop!

385
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:53,760
Idiot! We're this far in, we can't back out now!
Floor it and outrun them!

386
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:59,760
Aaaaaaah!

387
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:04,080
Aaaaaaah!

388
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:08,560
Aaaaaah!

389
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:17,960
It was just Buka's cute little prank, but
you're getting so worked up, it's annoying.

390
00:23:23,460 --> 00:23:26,600
Looks like something terrible has happened.

391
00:23:34,460 --> 00:23:35,640
Good morning.

392
00:23:40,080 --> 00:23:42,460
What happened, everyone?

393
00:23:43,440 --> 00:23:45,540
I've been thinking something over, you see.

394
00:23:45,540 --> 00:23:49,920
This time of year, a shaved head is
really the best, isn't it, Butcher?

395
00:23:49,920 --> 00:23:51,360
Shut up.

396
00:23:51,360 --> 00:23:54,120
Why should I and Nakagawa have to do it too,
all because of you?

397
00:23:54,120 --> 00:23:55,920
We've got to shave our heads.

398
00:23:57,600 --> 00:23:58,600
It's finished!

399
00:24:27,600 --> 00:24:30,580
Bursting with inspiration and bounce,

400
00:24:30,580 --> 00:24:33,480
gathering it all together and taking action,

401
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:34,960
and soaring away

402
00:24:34,960 --> 00:24:39,680
incredible power above all else

403
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:42,100
gather everyone

404
00:24:42,100 --> 00:24:45,620
if you come here

405
00:24:46,470 --> 00:24:51,940
the final energy, like a dream

406
00:24:53,130 --> 00:24:55,880
a star gazing at tomorrow

407
00:24:59,600 --> 00:25:03,040
the Kameari star spun
around in a full circle

408
00:25:05,580 --> 00:25:06,740
This should be fine, right?

409
00:25:06,740 --> 00:25:08,320
Like hell it's fine!

410
00:25:20,900 --> 00:25:24,360
Once again, the season of the
year-end bonus scramble has arrived.

411
00:25:24,360 --> 00:25:28,120
The shopping district folks are determined
to recover their debts from me this year,

412
00:25:28,120 --> 00:25:29,320
and it seems they've
been plotting a strategy,

413
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:32,080
but hah, I'm one step ahead of them!

414
00:25:32,580 --> 00:25:35,100
Next time: Bonus Scramble 3

415
00:25:35,100 --> 00:25:37,200
It's already the third one?

